    "ask": {"op":{"kind":"invoke","command":"judgment.assess","bind":"j","retry":null,"input":{"op":"object","fields":{"subject":{"op":"ref","root":"task","path":["subject"]},"question":{"op":"literal","value":"Classify this task: its kind of work, its risk, and four yes/no properties.\n\nKind of work: feature, bug fix (bugfix), refactor, test, docs, chore, sync, spec, design, implementation plan (plan), review of someone else's work (review), research, analysis, art or visual design (art), or repair of a failed integration or build (repair). Answer unknown if you cannot tell.\n\nRisk is how much damage the change could do if it is wrong. Judge it separately from how hard the work is, and from how well the task is written.\n- High risk: merging and publishing, CI gating, crash and session recovery, git branch handling, database migrations and stored data, authentication, permissions and secrets, money and live trading, deleting anything. Treat it as very high when a mistake would be hard to undo or would reach outside the repository.\n- Medium risk: ordinary changes to shared code that other work depends on.\n- Low risk: docs, UI copy, isolated components and tests, where a mistake is visible and cheap to undo.\nWhen a task touches several areas, go by the riskiest. When you can't tell, answer unknown.\n\n\"Narrow\" means the requirements are settled and the files to change are named or obvious. \"Covered by a test\" means an existing or specified test checks the result. Work that needs manual or end-to-end verification is not covered.\n\nNeeds deep reasoning: judge this from the task itself, not from how it was labelled or what level was asked for. It holds only when the work needs advanced mathematics or unusually hard reasoning. A big task is not a deep task, and neither is a risky one. Most tasks, including most specs, designs, plans and reviews, do not need this. Answer yes only if you can name what is unusually hard, and name it in the rationale.\nClearly harder: research that is clearly harder than ordinary research."},"context":{"op":"object","fields":{"items":{"op":"array","items":[{"op":"object","fields":{"label":{"op":"literal","value":"Title"},"text":{"op":"ref","root":"task","path":["facts","title"]}}},{"op":"object","fields":{"label":{"op":"literal","value":"Description"},"text":{"op":"ref","root":"task","path":["facts","description"]}}},{"op":"object","fields":{"label":{"op":"literal","value":"Kind given by whoever filed it"},"text":{"op":"ref","root":"task","path":["facts","kind"]}}}]}}},"fields":{"op":"literal","value":[{"id":"kind","description":"What kind of work the task is.","choices":["feature","bugfix","refactor","test","docs","chore","sync","spec","design","plan","review","research","analysis","art","repair","unknown"]},{"id":"risk","description":"How much damage the change could do if it is wrong.","choices":["low","medium","high","very_high","unknown"]}]},"flags":{"op":"literal","value":[{"id":"narrow","description":"The requirements are settled and the files to change are named or obvious."},{"id":"covered_by_test","description":"An existing or specified test checks the result. Work that needs manual or end-to-end verification is not covered."},{"id":"needs_deep_reasoning","description":"Judged from the task itself, not its label: the work needs advanced mathematics or unusually hard reasoning. Size and risk do not count. Most tasks, including most specs, designs, plans and reviews, do not need this. Answer yes only if you can name what is unusually hard."},{"id":"clearly_harder","description":"Research that is clearly harder than ordinary research."}]},"rationale_max_bytes":{"op":"literal","value":1024},"budget":{"op":"literal","value":{"deadline_ms":120000,"max_output_tokens":2048}}}}},"edges":{"accepted":"await","assessed":"assume","failed":"assume","refused":"assume"},"on_error":"assume"},
